    salaryContext: "Journeyman electricians earn $65,000–$95,000; master electricians and foremen $85,000–$130,000. Union electricians in major metros (New York, San Francisco) earn $110,000–$150,000 with benefits. Electrical contractors who pass the business cognitive demands earn $200,000+. Within the trade, IQ predicts advancement through the master electrician exam — a four-hour test covering the full NEC that has pass rates around 50%. Electricians who move into estimating, project management, or electrical engineering technology roles see income gains proportional to the additional cognitive demands of those positions.",
